  "description": "Read and write NC data of SINUMERIK controllers from your .NET code: axis positions, feed rates, R parameters, GUD variables and tool data, straight from the controller. Without DDE, without an HMI dependency, without an additional license. Stable in three-shift operation and in productive use at industrial customers.\n\nTNX-S stands for Traeger Numeric Exchange for Siemens.\n\nFeatures:\n• Read and write NC variables: axis positions, feed rates, channels, tools and mode groups\n• R parameters, GUD variables (LUD, GUD, PUD, MGUD, SGUD), DPR values and NSK/DEF symbols\n• Addressing in the familiar HMI Operate syntax: path (/Channel/...), token or alias from NSK\n• PDU-optimized access, KeepAlive, watchdog and connection pool\n• Automatic reconnect when the connection drops\n\nControllers & connectivity:\n• SINUMERIK 840D SolutionLine and SINUMERIK ONE natively over TCP/IP\n• SINUMERIK 840D PowerLine via an MPI/PROFIBUS-to-Ethernet adapter\n• One connection string per controller generation; IPv6 is supported\n\nTarget frameworks & platforms:\n• .NET Framework 4.7.2 and later\n• .NET Standard 2.0\n• .NET 10\n• C#, VB.NET and C++/CLI\n• Windows, Linux, macOS and Docker\n\nSDK variants:\nEvery tier includes all features of the tier below it.\n• Base package: all features listed above\n• Automation+: NC program upload/download and access to the controller's remote file system\n• Monitoring+: live stream via traces and conditions, high-frequency data changes, alarms and messages (DE, EN, FR, IT, ES built in, your own languages via a CSV or MBDDE COM file)\n• Production Pro: remote tool management, read and write tool tables, manage tool parameters\n• S7+ add-on for every tier: data blocks, flags and inputs/outputs of the integrated PLC\nOn SINUMERIK ONE, traces (live stream and high-frequency data changes) are not available, and alarms and messages additionally require the S7+ add-on.\n\nEvaluation, licensing & support:\n• Free, unlimited evaluation of all tiers: the trial license runs for 30 minutes per application start\n• Royalty-free: unlimited applications, no runtime fees per deployment\n• Support from the development team that builds and maintains the SDK",
